# React + TypeScript UI conventions

- Prefer functional components; colocate page-specific UI under `pages/` / feature folders
- Reuse `@ds` primitives (`Button`, inputs, badges) before inventing new base controls
- Keep forms accessible: labeled inputs, error text tied to fields, keyboard-friendly modals
- Mobile-first Tailwind; verify both 1440 and ~390 viewports for admin chrome
- Avoid purple-gradient / generic AI landing aesthetics on operational WMS screens
- Do not introduce Next.js App Router patterns — this app is Vite + React Router
- Prefer existing patterns in neighboring files over new abstractions
